# chan_oschan_spawn.tkr — the §10 OsChan fixed-width round-trip fixture. It proves the C0c AF_UNIX
# SOCK_DGRAM transport moves fixed-width i64 values across a real spawned thread boundary at the TEKO
# surface: a spawned producer sends 0..99 (i64) into the key-bound reader socket, the main thread
# recvfroms them until the zero-length Closed sentinel, and the round-trip sum (4950) is verified.
# Fixed-width T only (the datagram carries `elem_size` little-endian bytes); the generic OsChan<T>
# conformer + chan<T>::make DI surface is C3/C4, honest-stopped on the value-marshalling prerequisite.
# Linux-first (the abstract-namespace socket is Linux's). Runs on the C backend.

Feature: chan_oschan_spawn — a spawned worker sends, main recvs, i64 round-trip through an AF_UNIX datagram channel

  Scenario: producer_consumer_sum — 100 i64 sent by a worker thread, received by main, sum 4950
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
